@startuml
title PayLink - Refund a failed payment (FAILED -> REFUNDED)
' Names follow docs/design/glossary.md, architecture.md (section 4.1) and class-diagram.puml.
' Only the transitions of brief 2.5 are used: SENT_TO_BILLER -> FAILED, UNKNOWN -> FAILED, FAILED -> REFUNDED.
' Four ways to FAILED: biller refuses, later refusal, reconciliation, support confirms by hand (UC16).
' This diagram is for a FAILED payment. A refund after COMPLETED (FR-27) is a separate reversal: see seq-refund-completed.puml.

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
autonumber

actor "SupportUser" as Sup
participant "BillerAdapter" as Ad
participant "RetryCommand" as Retry
participant "ReconciliationService" as Rec
participant "PaymentService" as PS
participant "WalletService" as Wal
participant "NotificationObserver" as Notif

== 1. The payment becomes FAILED (four ways) ==
alt biller refuses (SENT_TO_BILLER -> FAILED, hard case 3)
  Ad -> PS : BillerOutcome REFUSED (error code)
  PS -> PS : status FAILED, reason = biller error code
else UNKNOWN payment: biller later refuses (UNKNOWN -> FAILED)
  Retry -> Ad : re-query after 1, 5 or 15 minutes
  Ad --> Retry : BillerOutcome REFUSED
  Retry -> PS : onBillerResult(reference, REFUSED)
  note right of PS
    A TopUpNet callback reaches `payments`
    through the same BillerCallbackListener.
  end note
  PS -> PS : status FAILED, reason = biller refused
else UNKNOWN payment: reconciliation finds no payment (UNKNOWN -> FAILED)
  Rec -> PS : payment is not in the settlement file
  PS -> PS : status FAILED, reason = not received by biller
else UNKNOWN payment: Support confirms the biller refused (UNKNOWN -> FAILED, UC16)
  Sup -> PS : resolveUnknown(paymentId, REFUSED)
  PS -> PS : status FAILED, reason = confirmed by support
  PS -> PS : AuditLog entry (who, when, why)
  note right of PS
    resolveUnknown works only on an UNKNOWN payment.
    With CONFIRMED the payment becomes COMPLETED instead
    (see the pay-a-bill diagram).
  end note
end
PS -> PS : write PaymentStatusHistory

== 2. Refund: hold released to the wallet (FAILED -> REFUNDED) ==
PS -> PS : refund(paymentId): find(paymentId)
alt status is not FAILED
  PS --> PS : refused, no money moves
  note right of PS
    UNKNOWN is never refunded automatically:
    money returns only once the system is sure
    the biller did not receive it.
    COMPLETED, REJECTED and REFUNDED are final.
  end note
else status is FAILED
  PS -> Wal : releaseHold(HoldId)
  alt hold already RELEASED (second request)
    Wal --> PS : nothing changed
    note right of Wal
      Releasing twice never credits twice
      (same idea as the idempotency key).
    end note
  else hold is ACTIVE
    Wal -> Wal : LedgerEntry HOLD_RELEASE\n(heldDelta = -total, availableDelta = +total)
    Wal -> Wal : Hold status RELEASED, AuditLog entry (who, when, why)
    note right of Wal
      The whole total comes back, including the fee:
      the fee was only held, never earned.
      No FEE_INCOME and no COMMISSION are posted.
    end note
    Wal --> PS : held -> available
    PS -> PS : status REFUNDED
    PS -> PS : write PaymentStatusHistory
  end
end

== 3. Notification (does not change the result, hard case 5) ==
PS ->> Notif : onPaymentEvent(PaymentEvent FAILED, then REFUNDED)
note right of Notif
  SMS and push with the clear reason (FR-22).
  A failed send is retried 3 times, then marked UNDELIVERED.
end note

== Related: settlement file lists a payment PayLink has as FAILED (hard case 7) ==
Rec -> Rec : ReconciliationDifference SETTLED_BUT_FAILED
note over Rec, PS
  Flagged in the ReconciliationReport for support to review.
  The system does not change the payment or the wallet by itself.
end note
@enduml
